        {
            "text": "The unit for $\\textit{Standard Atmosphere}$, symbol: $atm$, is an international reference pressure defined as $101.325 \\,kPa$ and formerly used as unit of pressure.\n  For practical purposes it has been replaced by the bar which is $100 kPa$. \n  The difference of about 1% is not significant for many applications, and is within the error range of common pressure gauges.",
